From c24df01553eeed985a5c79736f655e22b66dbc98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noobbbb2 <lees555@uos.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:15:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] robot: fixes from the first classroom run (2026-11-18,
 Foxy on the Jetson)

- install_foxy_jetson.sh: with OFB_FOXY_SNAPSHOT=1, add the snapshots.ros.org
  signing key (4B63...CBF125EA) and clear stale snapshot index files; the
  "Candidate" check no longer uses grep -q under pipefail (false "not found").
- env.sh: ofb_wait_topic tests the captured message instead of the pipeline
  status (BrokenPipeError from ros2 topic echo made /odom look missing);
  ofb_topic_hz stops `ros2 topic hz` with SIGINT so its output is flushed.
- Same grep -q / head pipeline pattern fixed in check_stage3/4/5, goto, objmem.
- bringup.sh: Foxy's robot.launch.py ignores LDS_MODEL and always starts the
  LDS-01 driver; with LDS-02 use the new robot/launch/robot_ld08.launch.py.
- udev: match SUBSYSTEM=="tty" so /dev/opencr and /dev/lidar point at the tty.
- check_stage4: no memory FAIL when a worker is already running; Ctrl+C stops
  the worker it started; worker_probe makes one untimed warm-up call.
- env_probe: objmem hint suggests `pip install -e . --no-deps`.
- README: the OpenCR firmware archive is gzip (tar -xzf).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
